 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law and the general municipal law, in\nrelation to prohibiting procurement of certain technology that poses security\nthreats; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2025 amending the state finance\nlaw and the general municipal law relating to prohibiting procurement of\ncertain technology that poses security threats, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 3259 and A. 2237, in relation to the authority of the office\nof information technology services to issue certain guidance relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S8793",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8793-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §163-e, St Fin L; amd §103-h, Gen Muni L; amd §§3 & 4, Chap of 2025 (as proposed in S.3259 & A.2237)",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8793\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law and the general municipal law, in\nrelation to prohibiting procurement of certain technology that poses\nsecurity threats; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2025 amending\nthe state finance law and the general municipal law relating to prohib-\niting procurement of certain technology that poses security threats, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 3259 and A. 2237, in relation\nto the authority of the office of information technology services to\nissue certain guidance relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2025, C.683.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by aligning the defi-\nnition of technology in these sections of law with an existing defi-\nnition of technology in the State Finance Law; limiting the ability to\ngrant waivers to the Office of Information Technology; requiring locali-\nties seeking federal waivers to inform the Office of Information Tech-\nnology; exempting from the ban any drones using United States maintained\nsoftware, that store their data in the US, and that prevent any compa-\nnies subject to the ban from accessing data; and requiring the Office of\nInformation Technology to issue the necessary guidance without having to\ngo through the formal regulations process.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 683 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that sections\none, two and three of this act shall take effect on the same date and in\nthe same manner as a Chapter of the Laws of 2025 amending the State\nFinance Law and the General Municipal Law relating to prohibiting\nprocurement of certain technology that poses security threats, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S.3259 and A.2237, takes effect.\n",
